  "body": "## What changed\n`structural::shell_structure_light` and `shell_structure_dark` failed intermittently in parallel ui runs (#605).\n- **Cause:** the live theme table `theme::LIVE` (read through `theme::current()`) is one per process. The structural and snapshot tests already serialise on `snapshot_guard()`, but `tests/theme_door.rs::the_theme_door_switches_the_theme_and_undo_restores_it` drives the real light → undo → redo → undo frame-edge sync without that lock, so it flips the shared table in the middle of a structural test.\n  - A flip to dark breaks `shell_structure_light` (\"frame-edge sync rode the world's reference\").\n  - A flip to light breaks `_dark`.\n- **Fix (tests only):** the theme-door switch test takes `snapshot_guard()`, and the `SNAPSHOT_LOCK` doc says any test whose frames move the world's theme must take it too.\n- **Why not per-harness:** the table is process-wide by design, read at ~44 sites with no `State` to hand. Making it per-harness would be a large production change for a race that exists only in tests.\n\n## How tested\n- **Before:** 30 parallel runs of `egui_app::tests::` gave 5/30 failures, all `shell_structure_light`. With the theme-door test skipped, 0/30, which confirmed the cause.\n- **After:** 0/30 on those runs, and 20 full parallel `camcraft-ui --lib` runs gave 0 structural or other failures. The headless-GPU test fails only on this machine.\n- Clippy is clean.\n\nChangelog: none (test-only)\n\nFixes #605\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
